\* TIER-2 CERT LEG — baseline liveness. EXPECT: clean drain, no temporal violation.
\*
\* Acceptance criterion (PROJECT_STATE §6): the second of the two baselines that must
\* reach a CONCLUSIVE verdict inside the time-box. A time-box exit is INCONCLUSIVE.
\*
\* NO SYMMETRY: TLC's symmetry reduction is unsound for temporal-property checking, and
\* the two temporal configs in this package (BaselineLiveness.cfg, Mut1Unservable.cfg)
\* have always omitted it. Preserved here deliberately — do not "harmonize" it in.
\*
\* This leg carries the F-LIVENESS-FAIR (§7.13) repair on the v0.10.4 model: `Progress`
\* was violated pre-repair, and the CLEAN DRAIN has never yet been observed at the large
\* bounds. If it drains clean here, that is a certified-at-reduced-bounds result and must
\* be stated as exactly that — it does NOT retire the large-bound obligation.
\*
\* @MAXMSGS@ is substituted by the tlc-cert workflow from the `cert_msgs` dispatch input.
SPECIFICATION Spec

CONSTRAINT
CertConstraint

CONSTANTS
Stages = {s1, s2}
MaxEpoch = 1
MaxRId = 1
MaxAttempt = 2
MaxPos = 1
MaxCrashes = 1
MaxMsgs = @MAXMSGS@
EnableUnservable = TRUE
ResetTruncates = TRUE
AttemptFencing = TRUE
AbortGuardEnabled = TRUE

INVARIANTS
Inv

PROPERTIES
Progress
PostDecisionLoss
EventualService
